__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.elc
.dgraph-pending.json
.dgraph-task-pending.json
.dgraph-edit.org

# Locks beside the two staging trays and the compose buffer, and the temp file
# `project.write_atomic` swaps in. All three are removed on the way out; what
# is ignored here is the one a `kill -9` leaves behind, which would otherwise
# be untracked and swept up by `git add -A`.
#
# Named one by one rather than swept up by `*.lock`, which is the rule this
# tool's own `project.IGNORE` states and this file was breaking: `*.lock` was
# quietly ignoring our `uv.lock`, so the lockfile had never been committed.
decisions.json.lock
tasks.json.lock
.dgraph-pending.json.lock
.dgraph-task-pending.json.lock
.dgraph-edit.org.lock
*.dg-tmp*
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/
.venv/
.pytest_cache/

# the demo renders into a work directory, but `dg render` inside demo/ would
# drop these here
demo/decision-graph.md
demo/tasks.md

# the detached web app: a run record and its output
.dgraph-serve.json
.dgraph-serve.log
